# Terminal rules
- When running Python scripts, ALWAYS redirect output to a temporary file and then read that file.
- Use this pattern: `python script.py > output.log 2>&1`
- After running, use read_file tool to read output.log
- Delete output.log when done
- Always use `conda run` instead of relying on active environment when possible
- Avoid commands that produce very long output. Use --quiet or -q flags when available
- Always use `python -u` flag to disable output buffering